## LED Indicator Reference

| LED Pattern | Meaning |
|-------------|---------|
| Red On | WiFi not connected |
| Yellow On (solid) | WiFi connected |
| Yellow Blinking | WiFi AP mode, waiting for connection |
| Green Blinking | Update available |
| Yellow + Green On | Update starting |
| Red Blinking | Update in progress |
| Red + Yellow + Green Sequence | Update successful |
| Multiple Red Flashes | Update error |
| Red + Yellow Alternating | Update error during flash |
| Brief Green Flash | Update check successful, update available |
| Brief Red Flash | Error checking for updates |
| Three Green Flashes | WiFi connection successful |
| Three Red Flashes | WiFi connection failed |
| Red + Green Flash | WiFi disconnection complete |

## Technical Implementation

The device implements a web server that provides various pages for configuration and updates. The firmware version is checked against a remote server, and updates are applied using the ESP32's built-in OTA functionality.

The code is structured to provide clear visual feedback at each stage of the process, making it ideal for educational purposes and understanding IoT device provisioning and update workflows.